+# Linear Issue Handler - Installation Guide
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+### 1. linearis CLI Tool
+
+The Linear Issue Handler skill requires the `linearis` command-line tool to interact with Linear's API.
+
+#### Installation
+
+Install the linearis CLI globally using npm:
+
+```bash
+npm install -g linearis
+```
+
+Or using yarn:
+
+```bash
+yarn global add linearis
+```
+
+#### Verify Installation
+
+Check that linearis is installed correctly:
+
+```bash
+linearis --version
+```
+
+### 2. Linear API Token
+
+You need a Linear API token to authenticate with Linear's API.
+
+#### Generate API Token
+
+1. Log in to your Linear account at [linear.app](https://linear.app)
+2. Go to Settings → API → Personal API keys
+3. Click "Create key" and give it a descriptive name (e.g., "Claude Code CLI")
+4. Copy the generated API token
+
+#### Configure API Token
+
+Create a file at `~/.linear_api_token` containing your API token:
+
+```bash
+echo "your_api_token_here" > ~/.linear_api_token
+chmod 600 ~/.linear_api_token
+```
+
+**Security Note:** The `chmod 600` command ensures only you can read the token file.
+
+#### Alternative: Environment Variable
+
+Alternatively, you can set the token as an environment variable (check linearis documentation for the correct variable name):
+
+```bash
+export LINEAR_API_KEY="your_api_token_here"
+```
+
+Add this to your shell configuration file (`.bashrc`, `.zshrc`, etc.) to persist across sessions.
+
+## Installing the Skill
+
+### For Claude Code
+
+1. **Download the skill file**:
+   ```bash
+   curl -o ~/.claude/skills/linear-issue-handler.md \
+     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trounceabout/skills-workshop/main/linear-issue-handler/SKILL.md
+   ```
+
+2. **Verify installation**:
+   ```bash
+   ls -la ~/.claude/skills/linear-issue-handler.md
+   ```
+
+### Manual Installation
+
+1. Create the skills directory if it doesn't exist:
+   ```bash
+   mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills
+   ```
+
+2. Copy the SKILL.md file to your Claude skills directory:
+   ```bash
+   cp linear-issue-handler/SKILL.md ~/.claude/skills/linear-issue-handler.md
+   ```
+
+## Verification
+
+Test that everything is set up correctly:
+
+1. **Test linearis CLI**:
+   ```bash
+   linearis --help
+   ```
+
+2. **Test API authentication**:
+   ```bash
+   linearis issues list
+   ```
+
+   This should list your Linear issues if authentication is working.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### "linearis: command not found"
+
+- Ensure linearis is installed: `npm install -g linearis`
+- Check that npm global bin directory is in your PATH
+- Try running `npx linearis --help` as an alternative
+
+### Authentication Errors
+
+- Verify your API token is correct in `~/.linear_api_token`
+- Ensure the token file has correct permissions: `chmod 600 ~/.linear_api_token`
+- Check that the token hasn't expired in Linear's settings
+- Try regenerating the API token
+
+### Permission Denied
+
+- Ensure you have write permissions to `~/.claude/skills/`
+- Check file permissions: `ls -la ~/.claude/skills/`
+
+## Next Steps
+
+Once installed, refer to the main [SKILL.md](SKILL.md) file for comprehensive usage documentation and workflow examples.
+
+## Version
+
+Current version: 1.0.0
+
+See [CHANGELOG](../releases/linear-issue-handler/CHANGELOG.md) for version history.
